      <li data-date="2023-02-27" data-tags="emacs org" data-cat="sw"><a href="https://michaelneuper.com/posts/replace-jupyter-notebook-with-emacs-org-mode/">Replace Jupyter Notebook With Emacs Org Mode</a></li>
      <li data-date="2023-01-09" data-tags="linux" data-cat="sw"><a href="https://michaelneuper.com/posts/what-linux-packaging-format-to-use/">Which Linux Packaging Format Should You Use?</a></li>
      <li data-date="2022-12-16" data-tags="linux security" data-cat="sec"><a href="https://michaelneuper.com/posts/enable-monitor-mode-on-tp-link/">Enable Monitor Mode on TP-Link TL-WN722N</a></li>
      <li data-date="2022-12-14" data-tags="security c" data-cat="sec"><a href="https://michaelneuper.com/posts/buffer-overflow/">Buffer Overflows: Keep Your Code Safe</a></li>
      <li data-date="2022-12-11" data-tags="linux" data-cat="sw"><a href="https://michaelneuper.com/posts/turning-a-window-manager-into-a-desktop-environment/">A Guide to Building Your Own Desktop Environment</a></li>
      <li data-date="2022-12-03" data-tags="web" data-cat="sw"><a href="https://michaelneuper.com/posts/how-to-create-your-own-website/">How to Create Your Own Static Website</a></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

